Z||000002||Groove Champion||10-08-2001||12:42 PM||||Performance improvements in Toronto should be able to help you out. The gauge usually doesn't cost more than $25. I got mine from there for about $18.<P>Take out the schrader valve on the fuel rail , this is covered by a little black cap. You may want to run the car and pull the fuel pump fuse to make sure there is no pressure , just to be safe.<P>Some of the gauges come with a small piece of metal line and the fittings , some don't. If you have ever hooked in NOS , this is basically the same procedure as putting in the fuel pressure saftey switch. You can leave the gauge attached to the rail, it won't hurt the performance of the car.<P>A leaky injector is hard to diagnose by using a gauge to read fuel pressure. It may be best to take the manifold off and pull the injectors out and have them cleaned , or clean them yourself. I have access to a ultrasonic cleaner I used to clean mine.  But you can send them out to have them cleaned as well. Performance improvements should know where to send them. <P><BR>Remember to replace the O-rings , it's just good piece of mind.<P>If performance improvements doesn't have a gauge , Try BC Auto. <P>GC.||||reg||1
